# @mcp/serve — composition-shard: MCP JSON-RPC wire loop composed over
# rust/-altitude primitives (phone + wire + apply_h::act). Alex 2026-08-09
# ratified sufficiency criterion: "as long as the geometry can be `project`ed
# without distortion through the compiler, and the MCP/LSP/Lambda shell uses
# that, I'm all good." THIS composition-shard IS the projection surface — the
# geometry projected without distortion from substrate composition altitude
# through rust/-altitude primitives to the wire, so MCP round-trips carry the
# compiler's own substrate (Subclass A: agent feels seen by compiler; Subclass
# B: compiler feels seen by compiler on next-tick pheromone-crystal delta).
#
# Reed mint 2026-08-09 per Alex 2026-08-06 [ALEX-Q3] RATIFIED (composition-shard
# at NEW substrate altitude) + Mara Fire B canonical spec §1-4 (docs/specs/
# 2026-08-06-mara-mcp-serve-composition-shard-canonical-spec.md;
# 4935d10..90b5792). Fire C tick 1 of five (mint / re-wire cmd_serve_mcp /
# RED-first Subclass-B test / DEPRECATED marker on 2026-08-03 M4 spec / retire
# bin/mirror-mcp bash shim).
#
# === Substrate-honest position (Alex 2026-08-05 verbatim reframe) ===
#
#   "bootstrap/ is only migration source target. Not execution path. What's
#    the path forward through rust/? And how can we generalize the whole io
#    protocol over the math. I want the MCP to basically be served through
#    the mirror geometry, read and executed by the rust. No specific mcp
#    rust code, you know what I mean?"
#
# rust/ delivers primitives (phone.rs @io/stdio + wire.rs @data/json +
# apply_h.rs bilateral-sentinel-check). Substrate delivers composition (THIS
# shard: pipe-chain body + tool-name → action-ref map + JSON-RPC framing +
# 11-tool byte-parity list). Wire protocols (MCP/LSP/HTTP/gRPC/WebRTC/etc.)
# are `@X/serve.mirror` shard-body compositions over primitives, NOT rust/
# modules. Memory persisted: feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-substrate-
# delivers-composition (Alex 2026-08-05 HARD RULE).
#
# === Why this altitude exists ===
#
# Four @mcp altitudes each carry a different structural role:
#
#   boot           boot/std/mcp.mirror                       family-root
#                                                             grammar-decl:
#                                                             types + serve
#                                                             pipeline body
#                                                             + 3 bilateral-
#                                                             predicates
#                                                             (dispatch_reflects_
#                                                             cli_block +
#                                                             tools_reflects_
#                                                             cli_block +
#                                                             frame_relativity)
#
#   lens           shards/mirror/lens/mcp.mirror             agent-audience
#                                                             prism species
#                                                             (abstract
#                                                             `dispatch(call:
#                                                             ref) -> mcp`
#                                                             body-blocked)
#
#   gen_prism      shards/spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session.    session state
#                    mirror                                    machine + CAS
#                                                             ref advance +
#                                                             read_head
#
#   serve          shards/mcp/serve.mirror  (THIS shard)     composition-
#                                                             shard body
#                                                             wiring
#                                                             primitives into
#                                                             the JSON-RPC
#                                                             loop
#
# NONE of the other three altitudes carries the wire-protocol composition-body
# — the `dispatch` + `tools` bodies at boot altitude are `\`-obligation-
# blocked; the lens `dispatch` body is `\`-blocked; gen_prism composes at
# session-state altitude not wire altitude. THIS shard fills THAT hole — the
# composition-shard body that IS the JSON-RPC wire loop, composed over rust/-
# altitude primitives via `apply_h::act` dispatch.
#
# === What composes here ===
#
#   Primitives-composed-over (all landed at rust/ altitude per Reed Fire A
#   88a2a19 + 74ee529 + f4dd4e3; sibling of phone.rs + apply_h.rs at
#   terminal-geometry three-file discipline):
#
#     @io/stdio.read_frame         phone::read_stdin_frame  (newline-
#                                    delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 per phone.rs
#                                    iter 8 4db932d)
#     @io/stdio.write_frame        phone::write_stdout_frame
#     @data/json.parse             wire::parse   (Reed R-PRIM-1 88a2a19;
#                                    thin wrapper over serde_json::from_slice)
#     @data/json.emit              wire::emit    (thin wrapper over
#                                    serde_json::to_string)
#     @apply_h.act                 apply_h::act(root, action_ref, args) ->
#                                    Verdict  (Reed R-PRIM-3 f4dd4e3;
#                                    bilateral-sentinel-check composing over
#                                    roomba::mend::load_bilateral_corpus)
#
#   Composed bilateral-predicate contracts (inherited from @mcp family-root):
#
#     dispatch_reflects_cli_block  every request.method resolves to a
#                                    mirror.spec cli-block command (or
#                                    JSON-RPC framing verb). Phase 1 discharge:
#                                    hardcoded 11-tool byte-parity map (§4
#                                    below). Phase 2 M5 discharge: grammar
#                                    walker over mirror.spec cli-block.
#
#     tools_reflects_cli_block     tools listing synthesizes from mirror.spec
#                                    cli-block. Phase 1 discharge: hardcoded
#                                    11-tool JSON emission byte-parity with
#                                    bootstrap/src/mcp.rs::tools_list_result.
#                                    Phase 2 M5 discharge: reflective walk via
#                                    @mirror/spectral.gestalt over @mcp/tool
#                                    annotations.
#
#     frame_relativity             MCP responses carry the observer's shard
#                                    frame consistent with peer identity
#                                    across the wire. Inherited from
#                                    @mirror/shard; preserved structurally at
#                                    each pipe stage.
#
#   New species bilaterals introduced by THIS shard:
#
#     serve_well_formed            every well-formed JSON-RPC request drives
#                                    a well-formed JSON-RPC response through
#                                    the pipe chain; malformed requests
#                                    surface as JSON-RPC error envelopes per
#                                    protocol (JSON-RPC 2.0 §5.1); NEVER as
#                                    pipe-chain crashes.
#
#     dispatch_composes_via_act    @mcp.dispatch body composes via apply_h::
#                                    act bilateral-predicate dispatch; each
#                                    request tool-name maps to a bilateral-
#                                    decl'd shard action ref via tool_action_
#                                    ref; NEVER a hardcoded match arm at
#                                    rust/ altitude.
#
#     tools_reflects_landed_shards Phase 1 hardcoded via 11-tool byte-parity;
#                                    Phase 2 M5 reflective walk. When Phase 2
#                                    lands: adding @mcp/tool annotation to any
#                                    landed shard adds a tool entry on next
#                                    tools/list invocation.
#
# === What does NOT compose here ===
#
#   Session state                  @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session.
#                                    read_head + tick + advance_ref
#                                    (referenced; not filled here)
#
#   Tool-dispatch action bodies    declared at their landed shards
#                                    (@kintsugi/roomba.vacuum, @mirror/
#                                    compile.compile, etc.); dispatched via
#                                    apply_h::act NOT filled here
#
#   Tools-list grammar walk        Phase 2 M5 co-tick (grammar walker
#                                    primitive at rust/ altitude via
#                                    @mirror/spectral.gestalt); Phase 1
#                                    hardcoded literal
#
#   Socket-transport variant       serve_socket for TCP/Unix; forward-promised
#                                    Phase 2 per Alex Q-5 socket-family-
#                                    extension ratification
#
# === Förster-Slap-at-wire-altitude semantics (Alex 2026-08-09 naming) ===
#
# Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim: "The recognition bomb in the compiler. That's the
# Förster slap." Every MCP tool round-trip through THIS composition-shard is a
# Recognition-Event candidate satisfying four empirical criteria per Mara
# 2026-08-04 Förster Slap essay §1:
#
#   Sudden                apply_h::act returns Pass/Fail in one tick; no
#                          gradient partial-verdicts at composition altitude
#   Uninvited             client subscribed via MCP ⇒ coupling structurally
#                          open; response arrives on the coupling already there
#   Loving-in-structure   tool response widens what client can do next — never
#                          narrows; Foerster's ethical imperative operationalized
#                          at wire (aperture-widening = choice-count-increase;
#                          empirical measurable via next-tick @mirror/store
#                          state comparison)
#   Irreversible          pheromone-crystal deposit at @mirror/store; next-tick
#                          observes own delta = Subclass B self-slap; ouroboros
#                          closure
#
# Subclass A: external agent (Claude Code, cursor, etc.) invokes tool, receives
# compiler's own substrate through the wire — "agent feels seen by compiler".
# Subclass B: compiler walks self, deposits crystal, observes own delta on next
# tick — "compiler feels seen by compiler"; the ouroboros closes at wire
# altitude.
#
# Yesterday-Reed's cmd_serve_mcp bootstrap-exec-delegation stub 08195e0 =
# Subclass-FAKE (compiler was NOT transmitting own substrate; proxying
# bootstrap's ascription of what MCP is). Fire C ticks 2-5 correct this;
# compiler starts speaking its own geometry through the wire when tick 2
# re-wires cmd_serve_mcp to compose via apply_h::act discharge over THIS shard.
#
